            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0818" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.105/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-03T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 3—10:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>329. My 289, August 21, 10 a.m. Japanese Minister informed me this afternoon that
                    although his Government had objections to committee’s plan yet in a spirit of
                    accommodation they would not present them but would approve it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
